%% Local snapshot read against a linearizable read (R106 addendum).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant T as Client thread (node B)
    participant B as Node B
    participant O as Owner of the term
    participant V as Voters
    rect rgba(127,127,127,0.12)
    Note over T,V: local snapshot read (no message)
    T->>B: new_transaction()
    B-->>T: snapshot of the newest committed root B knows (D46)
    Note over B: committed root learnt from done, release,<br/>own commits and permits (D50)<br/>may miss a commit acknowledged elsewhere<br/>a moment ago (R113)
    end
    rect rgba(127,127,127,0.12)
    Note over T,V: linearizable read: a barrier commit, then a snapshot (D46 amendment, Task 8.3n)
    T->>B: db.run(write one root, e.g. _read_barrier)
    B->>O: permit_req
    O-->>B: permit(base: newest root the owner knows committed, or a proposal)
    Note over B: base at or above every acknowledged commit (S4, R127)
    B->>V: replicate(barrier root on that base)
    V-->>B: majority acknowledges
    B-->>T: run() returns normally (unknown outcome or timeout raise: no barrier)
    T->>B: new_transaction()
    B-->>T: snapshot at or above the barrier root
    end
